# Refresh published engine measurements

## Root cause

The benchmark locks published engine releases. Its current pins are older than the registries, while the committed samples and charts record the old JavaScript lock hash and engine versions. Changing only the manifests would mislabel old measurements.

## Change

Update all three exact engine pins together. Reinstall the locked dependencies, rerun the shared JavaScript and full engine measurements on this host, and regenerate the reports and charts that derive from those samples.

## Scope

This updates engine provenance for every workload in the affected reports. No workload shape or parser special case drives the change.
